e>Malagelada</surname><given-names>J.-R.</given-names></name><name><surname>Stanghellini</surname><given-names>V.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Functional esophageal disorders</article-title><source>Gastroenterology</source><volume>130</volume><fpage>1459</fpage><lpage>1479</lpage><year>2006</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16678559</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Spencer</surname><given-names>C.M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Faulds</surname><given-names>D.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Lansoprazole: A reappraisal of its pharmacodynamic and pharmacokinetic properties, and its therapeutic efficacy in acid-related disorders</article-title><source>Drugs</source><volume>48</volume><fpage>404</fpage><lpage>430</lpage><year>1994</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7527761</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Petite</surname><given-names>J-P.</given-names></name><name><surname>Slama</surname><given-names>J-L.</given-names></name><name><surname>Licht</surname><given-names>H.</given-names></name><name><surname>Lemerez</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Coste</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name><name><surname>Andrieu</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Grimaud</surname><given-names>J.C.</given-names></name><name><surname>Julien</surname><given-names>H.</given-names></name><name><surname>Dupuis</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Sallerin</surname><given-names>V.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Comparison of Lansoprazole (30 mg) and omeprazole (20 mg) in the treatment of duodenal ulcers: A multicentric double-blind comparative trial</article-title><source>Gastroenterol. Clin. Biol.</source><volume>17</volume><fpage>334